# GitHub Copilot Instructions for {{projectName}}

## Project Architecture
This project uses the **{{pattern}}** architectural pattern with components under `{{basePath}}/`.

{{#if (eq pattern "atomic")}}
### Atomic Design
When generating component code, follow this directory structure:
- `{{basePath}}/components/atoms/ComponentName/` — Atoms
- `{{basePath}}/components/molecules/ComponentName/` — Molecules
- `{{basePath}}/components/organisms/ComponentName/` — Organisms
- `{{basePath}}/components/templates/ComponentName/` — Templates
- `{{basePath}}/components/pages/ComponentName/` — Pages
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq pattern "pages-components")}}
### Pages & Components
- `{{basePath}}/components/ComponentName/` — Reusable components
- `{{basePath}}/pages/ComponentName/` — Page-level components
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq pattern "feature-first")}}
### Feature-First
- `{{basePath}}/features/featureName/` — Feature modules with `components/`, `hooks/`, `utils/`, `index.ts`
- `{{basePath}}/shared/ComponentName/` — Shared components
{{/if}}

## Component Template
When creating a new component, always follow this exact structure:

```tsx
import React from 'react';
{{#if separateCss}}import styles from './ComponentName.module.css';{{/if}}

interface ComponentNameProps {
  children?: React.ReactNode;
}

export const ComponentName: React.FC<ComponentNameProps> = ({ children }) => {
  return (
    <div{{#if separateCss}} className={styles.container}{{/if}}>
      {children}
    </div>
  );
};
```

Each component directory must also include `index.ts`:
```ts
export { ComponentName } from './ComponentName';
```
{{#if includeTests}}
And a test file `ComponentName.test.tsx`:
```tsx
import React from 'react';
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import { ComponentName } from './ComponentName';

describe('ComponentName', () => {
  it('renders without crashing', () => {
    render(<ComponentName>Test Content</ComponentName>);
    expect(screen.getByText('Test Content')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```
{{/if}}

## Conventions
- **Exports**: Always named exports (no `export default`)
- **Typing**: Use TypeScript strictly; no `any`
- **Props**: Each component has a dedicated `{Name}Props` interface
{{#if separateCss}}- **Styles**: CSS Modules only (`*.module.css`), class name `container` for the root element{{/if}}
